+ 1 = 0 \\implies 1 + a - b + a + 1 = 0 \\implies 2a - b + 2 = 0 \\implies b = 2a + 2.\n\\]\n\n### Case 2: \\( r = -1 \\)\nSubstitute \\( r = -1 \\) into the polynomial:\n\\[\n(-1)^4 + a(-1)^3 - b(-1)^2 + a(-1) + 1 = 0 \\implies 1 - a - b - a + 1 = 0 \\implies -2a - b + 2 = 0 \\implies b = -2a + 2.\n\\]\n\n### Case 3: \\( r = \\omega \\) where \\( \\omega = e^{2\\pi i / 3} \\) (a primitive cube root of unity)\nThe roots of unity satisfy \\(\\omega^3 = 1\\) and \\(\\omega^2 + \\omega + 1 = 0\\). Substituting \\(\\omega\\) into the polynomial:\n\\[\n\\omega^4 + a\\omega^3 - b\\omega^2 + a\\omega + 1 = 0 \\implies \\omega + a - b\\omega^2 + a\\omega + 1 = 0 \\implies (1 + a)\\omega - b\\omega^2 + 1 = 0.\n\\]\nUsing \\(\\omega^2 = -1 - \\omega\\), we get:\n\\[\n(1 + a)\\omega - b(-1 - \\omega) + 1 = 0 \\implies (1 + a + b)\\omega + b + 1 = 0.\n\\]\nFor this to hold, both the real and imaginary parts must be zero. The real part is:\n\\[\nb + 1 = 0 \\implies b = -1,\n\\]\nand the imaginary part is:\n\\[\n1 + a + b = 0 \\implies 1 + a - 1 = 0 \\implies a = 0.\n\\]\nThus, \\((a, b) = (0, -1)\\).\n\n","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,10061,400,50,3,387,279,738,315,3501,4930,64,8402,15087,448,400,15,1124,273,264,4779,400,65,1124,273,220,16,3,1741,429,279,23606,198,78045,87,61,19,488,3859,61,18,481,44241,61,17,488,3859,488,220,16,284,220,15,59,60,4648,518,3245,825,1931,3704,13,220,29901,279,3082,315,279,4771,315,400,50,2418,151645,198,151644,77091,198,1249,8253,279,3082,315,279,738,17767,328,1124,8,315,3501,1124,1188,64,11,293,10699,8,1741,429,279,47311,17767,393,2075,8,284,856,61,19,488,3859,61,18,481,44241,61,17,488,3859,488,220,16,1124,8,702,518,3245,825,1931,3704,11,582,1191,553,41018,279,47311,323,1181,19703,382,5338,11,1077,594,9658,17767,435,1124,8,374,264,1931,3704,315,279,47311,17767,393,20